    "body": "(Copy pasted the relevant parts of the commit msg into the sections bellow)\r\n\r\nFound this while I was fuzzing the neovim UI with https://github.com/antithesishq/bombadil\r\n\r\n## Problem\r\n\r\nWhen the source buffer of `:InspectTree` or `:EditQuery` is hidden, an autocommand closes the tree and query windows that belong to it. If one of them was the last non-floating window, `nvim_win_close()` failed inside that autocommand with \"E444: Cannot close last window\". One way to get there is to turn the source window into a float and run :only from the tree window.\r\n\r\n## Solution\r\n\r\nclose_win() now leaves the last non-floating window open instead of trying to close it.",
    "closed_at": "2026-10-15T19:14:05Z",
    "comment_data": [],
